---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteNav from '../components/SiteNav.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Doc from '../components/Doc.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';

/**
 * Contact.
 *
 * Email only, on purpose. This site is static — there is no server behind it
 * that could receive a form submission — so a form here would either be
 * decorative or would quietly hand your message to a third party. A mailto is
 * honest about where the message goes.
 *
 * SETUP NOTE FOR THE SITE OWNER: `inbox` below is the only place the address
 * appears. Point it at the real mailbox once the domain's email is live.
 */
const inbox = 'hello@osiaffiliate.com';
---

<Layout
  title="Contact — OSI Affiliate"
  description="Email OSI Affiliate with a tool suggestion, a correction to a pricing line, or a question about whether a link on the site earns us anything."
>
  <SiteNav />
  <main>
    <PageHead
      title="Contact"
      lede="One address, read by a person. There is no contact form on this page because there is no server behind this site to receive one — a form here would be decoration."
    >
      <p class="mail">
        <Button href={`mailto:${inbox}`} variant="solid">Email {inbox}</Button>
      </p>
    </PageHead>

    <Doc>
      <section>
        <h2>What is worth writing about</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <b>A pricing line that has gone stale.</b> The most useful message we get. Vendors
            repackage constantly and we would rather hear it from you than leave it wrong.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>A tool we have left off a shortlist.</b> Tell us what you use and what it
            replaced. That second half is the part that changes our mind.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>A caveat you think is unfair.</b> Every pick carries a reason to skip it. If one
            of those is wrong about your experience, say so and we will look again.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Whether a specific link pays us.</b> Ask about any link on the site and we will
            answer it straight.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>A comparison you wanted and could not find.</b> New head-to-head pages get
            written where real demand shows up, and asking counts as demand.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>If you work for one of these vendors</h2>
        <p>
          Corrections about your own product are genuinely welcome, and we will fix a factual
          error quickly. What is not available at any price is placement: you cannot buy a slot
          on a shortlist, a higher position on one, or a change to the caveat in your entry. That
          is set out in full on the <a href="/disclosure">disclosure page</a>, and it does not
          move.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What we cannot do</h2>
        <p>
          We are not consultants, so we cannot run a bespoke evaluation of your business or sit
          on a procurement call. What we can do is tell you which of our picks we would choose in
          your situation and why — which is the same thing the pages do, with your specifics
          attached.
        </p>
        <p>
          We also cannot help with a vendor’s billing, account access or support queue. Those go
          to the vendor, who can actually see your account.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Before you write about a pick</h2>
        <p>
          The reasoning behind every shortlist is on <a href="/how-we-pick">how we pick</a>, and
          the money side is on the <a href="/disclosure">disclosure page</a>. If your question is
          “why is this tool here and not that one”, the answer may already be written down.
        </p>
      </section>
    </Doc>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>

<style>
  .mail {
    margin-top: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }
</style>
